{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel went and did.</b> But had they already done it? Was it not said to them from the first of the month? Rather, since they accepted it upon themselves, Scripture accounts it to them as though they did it (Mekhilta)." "<b>And they went and did.</b> Scripture even counts the going, to give reward for the going and reward for the doing (ibid.)." "<b>As YHWH commanded Moses and Aaron.</b> To declare their praise, that they omitted nothing of all the commandments of Moses and Aaron. And what is <b>so they did</b>? Moses and Aaron also did so (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:43.981180973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}